{
	"id": "catching-errors",
	"text": "Now, let's see how Effect deals with failure. First, we'll create safeDie, which wraps slowDie and recovers from its errors. To do this, we use catch, passing it a function that handles whatever error slowDie produces by returning another effect. We'll succeed with 0. And with that, the error type becomes never. Just as useful as knowing when and how something might fail is knowing that it cannot.",
	"code": "const slowDie: Effect.Effect<number, VeryBadRoll | TooHigh> =\n  Effect.gen(function* () {\n  \tconst n = yield* Random.nextIntBetween(1, 6)\n  \tyield* Effect.sleep(\"1 second\")\n  \tif (n === 4) yield* Effect.fail(new VeryBadRoll())\n  \tif (n === 6) yield* Effect.fail(new TooHigh())\n  \treturn n\n  })",
	"contentHash": "11f0a094793f4ca9",
